000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. SORTSIZE.
000300* The control statements the sort is handed. SORT-FILE-SIZE, when
000400* positive, is the SIZE=E estimate; each key's format follows
000500* from its usage: CH for alphanumerics and groups, ZD for DISPLAY
000600* numerics, PD for COMP-3, FI for COMP. The expected output is
000700* the sort's echo of what IBM ANS COBOL passed it on TK5, byte
000800* for byte.
000900 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001000 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001100 FILE-CONTROL.
001200     SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-SORTWK01.
001300 DATA DIVISION.
001400 FILE SECTION.
001500 SD  SORT-FILE.
001600 01  S-REC.
001700     05  S-G.
001800         10  S-G1 PIC X(3).
001900         10  S-G2 PIC 99.
002000     05  S-ZD     PIC S9(5).
002100     05  S-PD     PIC S9(7) COMP-3.
002200     05  S-FW     PIC S9(9) COMP.
002300     05  S-HW     PIC 9(4) COMP.
002400     05  S-X      PIC X(20).
002500 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002600 MAIN-PARA.
002700     MOVE 1333 TO SORT-FILE-SIZE.
002800     SORT SORT-FILE ASCENDING KEY S-G DESCENDING KEY S-ZD S-PD
002900         ON ASCENDING KEY S-FW S-HW S-X
003000         INPUT PROCEDURE IS NONE-IN OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS NONE-OUT.
003100     STOP RUN.
003200 NONE-IN SECTION.
003300 N1.
003400     EXIT.
003500 NONE-OUT SECTION.
003600 N2.
003700     RETURN SORT-FILE AT END DISPLAY 'NOTHING SORTED'.
